[b]Speculative Markets 1.2.1[/b]

[list]
[*]The Domestic Market News bulletin is redesigned. Its notice sums up the month in a sentence or two, and its tooltip names each good and interest group under its market sector.
[*]The Panic Risk alert now appears when Market Confidence would fall below the panic line if all of the Risks row's current risks struck at once. Before, it only counted every booming good collapsing together.
[*]With Better Politics Mod, its economic ideologies take a position on the Monetary Standard law.
[/list]

[b]Balance[/b]
[list]
[*]Leverage is now high risk, high reward. Each month of leverage gives 2% throughput and 0.5% investment up to 12 months, for at most 24% throughput and 6% investment (was 3.5% throughput up to 4 months, at most 14%, and no investment). Part months now count too.
[*]The leverage tooltips show the bonus and risk growing with every month, and what one more month would add.
[*]Bad Debts hit harder and last longer. Each point costs 3% throughput (was 3.5%) and 3.5% investment (was 0.75%), and the worst take about 6 years to clear (was 4).
[*]Reckless lending standards no longer cost trust each calm month (was 1 point a month). Large economies spend far less time Distrusted.
[*]A Trusted Exchange gives 5% prestige.
[/list]

On an existing save, older bulletins appear under Earlier News.
